{% extends "layout.njk" %}

{% block content %}

<h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Accessibility statement for Compliance Scraper</h1>

<p class="govuk-body">
  This accessibility statement applies to the Compliance Scraper service.
</p>
<p class="govuk-body">
  This service is run by the Department for Science, Innovation and Technology (DSIT). We want as many people as possible to be able to use this service.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">How accessible this service is</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
  This service is in alpha. We have built it using components from the GOV.UK Design System, which has been tested for accessibility. We believe the service is broadly compliant with the
  <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG21/">Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 AA</a>.
</p>
<p class="govuk-body">
  We have not yet commissioned a full independent accessibility audit. We plan to do this before the service moves to beta.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Reporting accessibility problems</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
  If you find any problems not listed on this page, or if you think we're not meeting accessibility requirements, contact us at
  <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:observability@dsit.gov.uk">observability@dsit.gov.uk</a>.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Enforcement procedure</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
  The Equality and Human Rights Commission (EHRC) is responsible for enforcing the Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2) Accessibility Regulations 2018. If you're not happy with how we respond to your complaint,
  <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.equalityadvisoryservice.com/">contact the Equality Advisory and Support Service (EASS)</a>.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Technical information about this service's accessibility</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
  DSIT is committed to making this service accessible, in accordance with the Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2) Accessibility Regulations 2018.
</p>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Compliance status</h3>

<p class="govuk-body">
  This service is <strong>partially compliant</strong> with WCAG 2.1 AA. The non-compliances and exemptions are listed below.
</p>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Non-accessible content</h3>

<p class="govuk-body">
  The following content is not fully accessible:
</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
  <li>The Insights chatbot page renders HTML responses directly in a chat bubble — this content has not been fully tested with assistive technologies.</li>
</ul>

<p class="govuk-body">
  We plan to fix these issues before the service moves to beta.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">What we're doing to improve accessibility</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
  We are working towards commissioning a full accessibility audit and will update this statement following that review.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Preparation of this accessibility statement</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
  This statement was prepared on <strong>22 April 2026</strong>. It was last reviewed on <strong>22 April 2026</strong>.
</p>
<p class="govuk-body">
  This service has not yet been tested against WCAG 2.1 AA by an independent body. The assessment was carried out internally by the DSIT Observability team.
</p>

{% endblock %}
